Bitmap JNI: no Perfetto track events on host

Not an upstream commit. Written for this build, from what the official library
shows.

Why: android-17.0.0_r1 libs/hwui/jni/Bitmap.cpp emits track events through the
Perfetto C SDK (003157f7d5c2 "Add bitmap tracing", later cb4a15248ece), and
libperfetto_c and libtracing_perfetto are on libandroid_runtime's host static_libs.
The official SDK 37 library (CLR2.260407.039) has no Perfetto code at all: none of
this file's slice names ("Bitmap_writeToParcel", "Bitmap_copyAshmemConfig",
"bitmap_copy"), no PerfettoTe or track_event strings, and no Perfetto imports.
So its build of this file has these calls compiled out, by a change we cannot
see in public history (r1 is the newest public source). Doing the same keeps the
SDK out of the library. The slices have no consumer on host.

--- a/libs/hwui/jni/Bitmap.cpp
+++ b/libs/hwui/jni/Bitmap.cpp
@@ -39,6 +39,7 @@
 #include "android/binder_parcel.h"
 #endif
 #include "android_nio_utils.h"
+#ifdef __ANDROID__
 #include "perfetto/public/abi/track_event_abi.h"
 #include "perfetto/public/producer.h"
 #include "perfetto/public/protos/trace/track_event/track_event.pzc.h"
@@ -46,6 +47,7 @@
 #include "perfetto/public/te_macros.h"
 #include "perfetto/public/track_event.h"
 #include "trace_categories.h"
+#endif
 
 #define DEBUG_PARCEL 0
 
@@ -182,6 +184,7 @@
 
